From 15741f489f94626d2bae84d3dc391cf474e7cf67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:18:38 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 072/230] Pin A-ADS unit to the viewport bottom so the app
 can't cover it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The React shell was overlapping the static ad, which A-ADS rejects as
"partly or fully hidden". Fix the wrapper to the bottom center with a
high z-index and add a spacer below it so app content never sits behind
the ad.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
---
 index.html | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index b7d5ac9..3620876 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -98,7 +98,17 @@
     <!-- BEGIN AADS AD UNIT 2458182 -->
     <div
       id="aads-frame"
-      style="margin: 16px auto; max-width: 468px; padding-bottom: 80px; position: relative; z-index: 1"
+      style="
+        position: fixed;
+        bottom: 0;
+        left: 50%;
+        transform: translateX(-50%);
+        width: 100%;
+        max-width: 468px;
+        z-index: 9999;
+        background: transparent;
+        padding: 8px 0;
+      "
     >
       <iframe
         data-aa="2458182"
@@ -114,6 +124,8 @@
         "
       ></iframe>
     </div>
+    <!-- Spacer so the app's content doesn't hide behind the fixed ad. -->
+    <div style="height: 80px; width: 100%"></div>
     <!-- END AADS AD UNIT 2458182 -->
   </body>
 </html>
